menu "NFC Card Storage"

    config KERN_NFC
        bool "Enable NFC card storage (M5Stack RFID Unit 2 / WS1850S)"
        default y
        help
            Compile support for keeping KEF-encrypted mnemonics on NFC cards,
            read and written through a WS1850S module on the board's I2C bus.

            Building it in does not turn it on: the feature stays inert until
            it is also enabled at runtime under Settings -> NFC, which is off
            by default. The RF field is energized only while the card page is
            open.

    config KERN_NFC_I2C_ADDR
        hex "WS1850S I2C address"
        default 0x28
        depends on KERN_NFC
        help
            7-bit I2C address of the reader. 0x28 is the M5Stack RFID Unit 2
            factory default.

    config KERN_NFC_I2C_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "I2C transaction timeout (ms)"
        default 100
        depends on KERN_NFC
        help
            Per-transfer timeout for reader register access. Bounds every
            blocking call so an absent or wedged module cannot stall the UI.

endmenu
